    "key": "s1",
    "heading": "Two shots turn the table gap upside down",
    "paragraphs": [
     "Sporting Kansas City arrived at Shell Energy Stadium in 30th place and left with a victory over a Houston Dynamo FC side sitting sixth. The upset took shape through a stark first-half contrast: Houston Dynamo FC attempted seven shots, but Sporting Kansas City scored from each of its two efforts.",
     "André Luiz supplied the opening goal in the 27th minute. Houston Dynamo FC had recorded three shots by the end of the opening half-hour without putting one on target, while André Luiz converted Sporting Kansas City’s first attempt of the match. Calvin Harris then struck in the 45th minute, sending the visitors into the interval with a two-goal lead. Both Sporting Kansas City shots before the break were on target; Houston Dynamo FC put two of seven on target without scoring."
    ]
   },
   {
    "key": "s2",
    "heading": "Herrera’s red card changes the second-half picture",
    "paragraphs": [
     "Héctor Herrera was shown a red card in the 46th minute, leaving Houston Dynamo FC to play the second half with 10 players. The dismissal did not reduce the home side’s shooting volume: it produced 14 attempts after the break, including 11 between the 61st and 75th minutes. Only two of those second-half shots tested the goalkeeper, however, and neither changed the score.",
     "Houston Dynamo FC introduced Felipe Andrade for Franco Negri in the 56th minute, then made three changes in the 71st as Matthew Arana, Marcelo Saracchi and Lyle Foster replaced Agustín Bouzat, Lawrence Ennali and Ibrahim Aliyu. Sporting Kansas City removed André Luiz for Ruben Ramos in the 63rd minute and later replaced Harris with Owen Wolff in the 72nd. The visitors also recorded eight second-half attempts, two of them on target, but all the scoring remained confined to the first half."
    ]
   },
   {
    "key": "s3",
    "heading": "Harris and André Luiz make limited openings count",
    "paragraphs": [
     "The two scorers produced different shooting lines. André Luiz took three attempts overall, two from inside the penalty area, and scored with his only shot on target. Harris attempted two shots and put both on target, with one coming from inside the box. Together, their finishing gave Sporting Kansas City the return that Houston Dynamo FC could not find from a much larger collection of attempts.",
     "Guilherme Augusto was Houston Dynamo FC’s most frequent shooter with six attempts, but only one was on target and two came from inside the area. Bouzat, Antônio Carlos and Herrera also registered one shot on target apiece. Ibrahim Aliyu, Lucas Halter and Mateusz Bogusz each attempted two shots without hitting the target, illustrating how the home side’s activity repeatedly ended away from the goalkeeper."
    ]
